WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:05.150
At night you can’t see shapes or numbers, so the lights have to carry the message.

2
00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:07.200
The rule is simple.

3
00:00:07.450 --> 00:00:09.625
Red marks show red lights.

4
00:00:09.875 --> 00:00:12.050
Green marks show green lights.

5
00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:16.500
The rhythm can be flashing, occulting, quick, or isophase.

6
00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:19.650
A quick-flashing light means pay attention.

7
00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:25.350
It usually marks a sharp turn, a junction, or a spot that needs special caution.

8
00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:28.825
Lighted buoys usually aren’t nun or can shaped.

9
00:00:29.075 --> 00:00:31.175
They’re pillars or spars.

10
00:00:31.425 --> 00:00:34.325
So how do you tell red from green in daylight?

11
00:00:35.325 --> 00:00:37.875
By color and number, not shape.

12
00:00:38.125 --> 00:00:48.000
And a preferred channel mark, where a channel splits, shows a special rhythm: composite group flashing, two flashes and then one, in the color of its top band.

13
00:00:48.250 --> 00:00:49.975
One more tip.

14
00:00:50.225 --> 00:00:54.050
Unlighted buoys carry reflective tape in their own color.

15
00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:56.450
A spotlight will pick them out.
